# Child's Play (jeuno 23): the kinds of Karl's replies, against Lure of the Wildcat (Jeuno)'s. Karl has no script; Lure
# of the Wildcat (Jeuno) accepted (a GM, before login) answers him with 316 (a progressEvent) while its Prog bit 16 is
# clear, and its finish sets the bit (cleared again by a GM). A level 75 Warrior, The Wonder Magic Set accepted (a GM).
# Available: 0 and 316, both progressEvents, tie: the lookup plays the first in its list, Child's Play's 0 (an event 0
# would lose to 316); 0 begins the quest. Accepted: 316 (a progressEvent) beats 61 (an event; a progressEvent 61 would
# tie with 316 and play first), every time.
lists PortJeuno/Karl/onTrigger PortJeuno/onEventFinish/0 PortJeuno/onEventFinish/316
char zone=PortJeuno pos=-59.4,0,-8.9 job=WAR lvl=75
quest Jeuno.TheWonderMagicSet accepted
quest Jeuno.LureOfTheWildcat accepted
login
trigger Karl                            # available: 0 and 316 tie: 0, the first in the list
finish                                  # begun
trigger Karl                            # accepted: 316 over 61
finish                                  # the Wildcat's bit 16
charvar Quest[3][90]Prog 0              # a GM: the bit clear
trigger Karl                            # 316 over 61
finish
charvar Quest[3][90]Prog 0              # a GM
trigger Karl                            # 316 over 61
finish
